    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9470c59f-1031-59e5-a515-ce29f2b8745e" activityNameId="506b295b-7aa0-58ed-acea-351a1b893e62" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, AEC, Balance of Plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, AEC, Balance of Plant
1 MWe AEC electrolyzer Blance of Plnat, based on Niklas Gerloff, Comparative Life-Cycle-Assessment analysis of three major water electrolysis technologies while applying various energy scenarios for a greener hydrogen production, Journal of Energy Storage, Volume 43, 2021, https://doi.org/10.1/j.est0.20.1. Produced amount of H2 over 20 years: 4,259,200 kg. The technology is available for large plant sizes and operates with a stack efficiency of up to 67 % (based on the lower heating value (LHV) of the generated H2). The operating temperature is in between 60â€“80â€¯Â°C, and the current density is around 0.2â€“0.4â€¯A/cm2. Moreover, the system energy â€“including the stack and periphery energyâ€“ is in the range of 4.4â€“6.6â€¯kWh/m3H2, while the gas purity is higher than 99.5%, and the operating pressure is below 30â€¯bar. While the LCI data of the BoP components either originate from Zhang et al., based on a 300-kW system and, therefore, scaled-up to 1â€¯MW by a factor of 0.7, the LCI data of the other BoP components originate from manufacturer offers or have been estimated by own calculations using additional information by the producers. For additional specifications, refer to Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: ec3912ad-d37f-3bb2-9f47-f1aff5b50f95
Location: 
